{"duration_api_ms":185842,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"9a46d453-15e2-4815-a87e-da98a895c393","total_cost_usd":2.00713,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67413,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":13177,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8066},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67413,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13177,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":67413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":67413},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-fable-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13177,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":67413,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.00713,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":8066,"canonicalModel":"claude-fable-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"candidate_id\":\"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731ff3a60283\",\"run_id\":\"a219d556-531c-4bf1-b25a-2f6350cbb45d\",\"packet_sha256\":\"9f28619033a2fd67813dcd78201c74099d830bdc10ae69982c44b085384d956d\",\"schema\":\"agent-ee.review/1\",\"role\":\"physical\",\"coverage\":[\"Re-derived the RC step response analytically: R1=10k, C1=100n gives tau=1 ms and V(1 ms)=1-exp(-1)=0.63212 V; the ngspice measurement 0.6321201 V (work/rc-step/ngspice.log) matches and sits inside the declared 0.62-0.65 V band from inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md.\",\"Audited the simulation deck (work/rc-step/deck.cir, work/rc-step/control.sp): element values and topology (C1 OUT-0, R1 IN-OUT, PWL 1 ns-rise 1 V step, .tran 0.005m 5m) match the schematic netlist; exclusion of connector J1 is consistent with the declared unloaded-response requirement.\",\"Hand-traced schematic wires, local labels and power symbols in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch by coordinate and confirmed the exported netlist (work/netlist/design.xml, work/netlist/connectivity.json): /IN={J1.1,R1.1}, /OUT={C1.1,J1.2,R1.2}, GND={C1.2,J1.3}.\",\"Checked every pad net assignment and position in inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb against the netlist and verified all five track segments' endpoints land on pad centers or on same-net copper, including the /OUT T-junction at (107.5,100) onto the segment between R1.2 (105.9125,100) and C1.1 (109.05,100).\",\"Verified the saved B.Cu GND zone filled_polygon is consistent with current geometry (not stale): roundrect clearance cutout 98.65-101.35 mm around J1 pad 1 (rect 1.7 mm + 0.5 mm clearance), 1.35 mm radius circular cutout around J1 pad 2 at (100,102.54), thermal-relief spokes around J1 pad 3 at (100,105.08), and solid fill at the GND via (113,100).\",\"Independently confirmed all 5 track segments are 0.25 mm wide in the native board file, meeting the declared 0.20 mm minimum (work/geometry/geometry.json agrees); confirmed the probe's 5-segment count is complete (sixth track item is the via).\",\"Checked placement and board-edge margins: courtyards (J1 98.23-101.77 x / 98.23-106.85 y; R1 103.32-106.68 x; C1 108.3-111.7 x) do not overlap and sit inside the 96-116 x 96-108 mm Edge.Cuts outline; zone outline is 0.5 mm inside the edge; via at (113,100) is 3 mm from the nearest edge.\",\"Checked F.Cu clearances by coordinate: the /OUT track at y=102.54 clears J1 pad 3 (GND) by ~1.6 mm; the /OUT vertical segment at x=107.5 clears R1.2 and C1.1 pad edges by ~0.9-1.1 mm; GND and /OUT tracks at y=100 are separated by same-net or >1.5 mm gaps.\",\"Assessed current/thermal plausibility: with a 1 V source into 10 kohm the maximum current is ~0.1 mA, so 0.25 mm tracks, the 0.6/0.3 mm via and 0.5 mm thermal spokes are not electrically stressed; no thermal qualification is claimed or needed to be inferred.\",\"Cross-checked check records for internal consistency: board_sha256 in work/drc/execution-details and work/geometry match the supplied inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb hash f8264d95...; ERC/DRC consoles match their recorded hashes and report zero violations, zero unconnected items, zero parity issues.\"],\"limitations\":[\"Tool-free review: I could not refill the zone, re-run DRC/ERC/ngspice, or open work/rc-step/result.raw (binary, retained for operator); electrical conclusions rest on the logged .meas values plus my independent analytic calculation.\",\"The thermal-spoke region of the saved zone polygon around J1 pad 3 was checked for plausibility and position, but spoke continuity was not re-computed geometrically point-by-point; I rely partly on DRC's zero unconnected items for final zone connectivity.\",\"No fabrication capability spec was declared beyond the 0.20 mm track-width criterion, so via annular ring (0.15 mm), 0.3 mm drill, zone clearances and hole-to-edge distances were assessed only for plausibility, not against a fab rule set.\",\"Component tolerance, temperature, loading, ADC sampling, EMI and real hardware behavior are untested, as declared in the packet; I did not attempt to extend coverage beyond noting the gaps.\",\"Solder paste, silkscreen legibility and 3D/assembly interference were reviewed only via coordinates in the native files, not rendered outputs; no gerber/fab outputs were in the packet.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"PHY-01\",\"title\":\"GND return between C1 and connector depends on a single 0.3 mm-drill via plus zone thermal spokes\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb — via uuid b71a70d7-bbc1-43d1-ae55-5e4d992412a4 at (113,100); zone uuid 38a83012-bcf9-4bb9-b9f4-50d49cd91d90 (B.Cu, thermal_bridge_width 0.5); pad J1.3 uuid ddcb81c6-a965-456f-b8c7-71a870b91a1d\",\"condition\":\"GND exists on F.Cu only as the 2.05 mm track from C1 pad 2 to one 0.6 mm/0.3 mm via; all continuity to J1 pin 3 runs through the B.Cu zone and the 0.5 mm thermal-relief spokes at J1 pad 3. There is no redundant via or direct F.Cu GND route.\",\"mechanism\":\"A single manufacturing or mechanical defect in the via barrel (0.15 mm annular ring) or a broken thermal spoke opens the only return path, leaving C1's ground floating relative to the connector and invalidating the filter output reference at J1. At the fixture's ~0.1 mA signal level there is no ampacity issue, but there is no redundancy.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"segment uuid 7deb1fb0 (110.95,100)-(113,100) net GND; via uuid b71a70d7 size 0.6 drill 0.3; zone uuid 38a83012 thermal_gap 0.5 thermal_bridge_width 0.5\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"tracks[] via entry width_mm 0.6 drill_mm 0.3; nets GND count 2; zones[0] net GND layers B.Cu\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"unconnected_items: [] (connectivity as saved is complete)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Verified connectivity is intact in the saved file (zone fill cutouts and spoke geometry match current pad positions, DRC reports zero unconnected items), so this is not a defect. It is a robustness observation appropriate to a disposable fixture: acceptable here, but worth knowing the GND net has exactly one inter-layer path and no declared fab criterion covers the 0.15 mm annular ring.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-02\",\"title\":\"vout_5ms measurement has no limits and contributes nothing to the pass verdict\",\"location\":\"packet criteria rc-step / work/rc-step results\",\"condition\":\"The rc_transient criterion declares measurement vout_5ms at 5 ms with min and max both null; the check records measured 0.9932621 with within_limits absent, yet the overall rc-step outcome is 'pass — meets all declared measurement limits'.\",\"mechanism\":\"An unconstrained measurement is logged but never compared against anything, so the settled-value behavior (expected ~0.9933 = 1-exp(-5)) is observed but not verified. Any settled value — including one revealing a wrong C or a loading error — would still yield 'pass' as long as the 1 ms point happened to land in band. This weakens the apparent verification coverage of the step response.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"vout_5ms = 9.932621e-01 (no limit comparison)\"},{\"path\":\"work/rc-step/deck.cir\",\"locator\":\".meas tran vout_5ms FIND v(OUT) AT=5m\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 1 constrains only V(/OUT) at t=1 ms\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The measured 5 ms value does independently match my analytic expectation (1-exp(-5)=0.99326), so no electrical problem is indicated. But as a coverage critique: the declared requirements only bound the 1 ms point, and the extra measurement gives an illusion of broader checking while enforcing nothing. Flagged so the pass verdict is read as verifying exactly one point on the curve.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-03\",\"title\":\"Geometry criterion covers track segments only; vias, zone copper and clearances are checked solely against KiCad defaults\",\"location\":\"packet criteria geometry (min_track_width_mm 0.2); inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb setup section\",\"condition\":\"The declared 0.20 mm geometry requirement applies to track segments (all 5 are 0.25 mm, verified). The via (0.6 mm pad / 0.3 mm drill, 0.15 mm annular ring), the zone's 0.25 mm min_thickness, pad-to-track clearances and hole-to-edge distances are governed only by the board's default DRC rules; the .kicad_pcb setup section defines no explicit net classes or custom constraint rules.\",\"mechanism\":\"DRC passing with default rules demonstrates internal consistency, not manufacturability at a specific fab. If this fixture is actually fabricated, features like the 0.15 mm annular ring may violate a vendor's capability even though every declared criterion and DRC check passes. A successful DRC exit is not proof the board can be built to spec by an arbitrary vendor.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"narrowest_mm 0.25 across 5 segments; via width_mm 0.6 drill_mm 0.3 not subject to the width criterion; zones[0].min_thickness_mm 0.25\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_pcb\",\"locator\":\"(setup ...) block: no net classes or custom design rules declared; via uuid b71a70d7 (size 0.6 drill 0.3)\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements/fixture-requirements.md\",\"locator\":\"requirement 2: track-segment width only, explicitly 'not an ampacity or manufacturing guarantee'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The requirements document itself scopes requirement 2 to track segments and disclaims manufacturing guarantees, so this is not a violation of anything declared — hence a concern, not a defect, at info severity. It is recorded so that the all-green check set is not mistaken for fabrication qualification of the via, zone and clearance geometry.\"}]}","structured_output":{"candidate_id":"7b6d5a949427df9a9100abf2208581f5564cf9ec758e1b0f1fbe731ff3a60283","run_id":"a219d556-531c-4bf1-b25a-2f6350cbb45d","packet_sha256":"9f28619033a2fd67813dcd78201c74099d830bdc10ae69982c44b085384d956d","schema":"agent-ee.review/1","role":"physical","coverage":["Re-derived the RC step response analytically: R1=10k, C1=100n gives tau=1 ms and V(1 ms)=1-exp(-1)=0.63212 V; the ngspice measurement 0.6321201 V (work/rc-step/ngspice.log) matches and sits in